#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:236
msgid ""
"Ajv compiles schemas to functions and caches them in all cases (using "
"schema serialized with [fast-json-stable-"
"stringify](https://github.com/epoberezkin/fast-json-stable-stringify) or "
"a custom function as a key), so that the next time the same schema is "
"used (not necessarily the same object instance) it won't be compiled "
"again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:238
msgid ""
"The best performance is achieved when using compiled functions returned "
"by `compile` or `getSchema` methods (there is no additional function "
"call)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:240
msgid ""
"__Please note__: every time a validation function or `ajv.validate` are "
"called `errors` property is overwritten. You need to copy `errors` array "
"reference to another variable if you want to use it later (e.g., in the "
"callback). See [Validation errors](#validation-errors)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:242
msgid ""
"__Note for TypeScript users__: `ajv` provides its own TypeScript "
"declarations out of the box, so you don't need to install the deprecated "
"`@types/ajv` module."
msgstr ""

