#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:295
msgid "Validation keywords"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:297
msgid ""
"Ajv supports all validation keywords from draft-07 of JSON Schema "
"standard:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:299
msgid "[type](https://github.com/ajv-validator/ajv/blob/master/KEYWORDS.md#type)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:300
msgid ""
"[for numbers](https://github.com/ajv-"
"validator/ajv/blob/master/KEYWORDS.md#keywords-for-numbers) - maximum, "
"minimum, exclusiveMaximum, exclusiveMinimum, multipleOf"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:301
msgid ""
"[for strings](https://github.com/ajv-"
"validator/ajv/blob/master/KEYWORDS.md#keywords-for-strings) - maxLength, "
"minLength, pattern, format"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:302
msgid ""
"[for arrays](https://github.com/ajv-validator/ajv/blob/master/KEYWORDS.md"
"#keywords-for-arrays) - maxItems, minItems, uniqueItems, items, "
"additionalItems, [contains](https://github.com/ajv-"
"validator/ajv/blob/master/KEYWORDS.md#contains)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:303
msgid ""
"[for objects](https://github.com/ajv-"
"validator/ajv/blob/master/KEYWORDS.md#keywords-for-objects) - "
"maxProperties, minProperties, required, properties, patternProperties, "
"additionalProperties, dependencies, [propertyNames](https://github.com"
"/ajv-validator/ajv/blob/master/KEYWORDS.md#propertynames)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:304
msgid ""
"[for all types](https://github.com/ajv-"
"validator/ajv/blob/master/KEYWORDS.md#keywords-for-all-types) - enum, "
"[const](https://github.com/ajv-"
"validator/ajv/blob/master/KEYWORDS.md#const)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:305
msgid ""
"[compound keywords](https://github.com/ajv-"
"validator/ajv/blob/master/KEYWORDS.md#compound-keywords) - not, oneOf, "
"anyOf, allOf, [if/then/else](https://github.com/ajv-"
"validator/ajv/blob/master/KEYWORDS.md#ifthenelse)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:307
msgid ""
"With [ajv-keywords](https://github.com/ajv-validator/ajv-keywords) "
"package Ajv also supports validation keywords from [JSON Schema extension"
" proposals](https://github.com/json-schema/json-schema/wiki/v5-Proposals)"
" for JSON Schema standard:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:309
msgid ""
"[patternRequired](https://github.com/ajv-"
"validator/ajv/blob/master/KEYWORDS.md#patternrequired-proposed) - like "
"`required` but with patterns that some property should match."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:310
msgid ""
"[formatMaximum, formatMinimum, formatExclusiveMaximum, "
"formatExclusiveMinimum](https://github.com/ajv-"
"validator/ajv/blob/master/KEYWORDS.md#formatmaximum--formatminimum-and-"
"exclusiveformatmaximum--exclusiveformatminimum-proposed) - setting limits"
" for date, time, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:312
msgid ""
"See [JSON Schema validation keywords](https://github.com/ajv-"
"validator/ajv/blob/master/KEYWORDS.md) for more details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:315
msgid "Annotation keywords"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:317
msgid ""
"JSON Schema specification defines several annotation keywords that "
"describe schema itself but do not perform any validation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:319
msgid ""
"`title` and `description`: information about the data represented by that"
" schema"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:320
msgid ""
"`$comment` (NEW in draft-07): information for developers. With option "
"`$comment` Ajv logs or passes the comment string to the user-supplied "
"function. See [Options](#options)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:321
msgid ""
"`default`: a default value of the data instance, see [Assigning defaults"
"](#assigning-defaults)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:322
msgid ""
"`examples` (NEW in draft-06): an array of data instances. Ajv does not "
"check the validity of these instances against the schema."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:323
msgid ""
"`readOnly` and `writeOnly` (NEW in draft-07): marks data-instance as "
"read-only or write-only in relation to the source of the data (database, "
"api, etc.)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:324
msgid ""
"`contentEncoding`: [RFC "
"2045](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2045#section-6.1 ), e.g., "
"\"base64\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:325
msgid ""
"`contentMediaType`: [RFC 2046](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2046), "
"e.g., \"image/png\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:327
msgid ""
"__Please note__:  Ajv does not implement validation of the keywords "
"`examples`, `contentEncoding` and `contentMediaType` but it reserves "
"them. If you want to create a plugin that implements some of them, it "
"should remove these keywords from the instance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:330
msgid "Formats"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:332
msgid ""
"Ajv implements formats defined by JSON Schema specification and several "
"other formats. It is recommended NOT to use \"format\" keyword "
"implementations with untrusted data, as they use potentially unsafe "
"regular expressions - see [ReDoS attack](#redos-attack)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:334
msgid ""
"__Please note__: if you need to use \"format\" keyword to validate "
"untrusted data, you MUST assess their suitability and safety for your "
"validation scenarios."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:336
msgid ""
"The following formats are implemented for string validation with "
"\"format\" keyword:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:338
msgid ""
"_date_: full-date according to "
"[RFC3339](http://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc3339#section-5.6)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:339
msgid "_time_: time with optional time-zone."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:340
msgid ""
"_date-time_: date-time from the same source (time-zone is mandatory). "
"`date`, `time` and `date-time` validate ranges in `full` mode and only "
"regexp in `fast` mode (see [options](#options))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:341
msgid "_uri_: full URI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:342
msgid "_uri-reference_: URI reference, including full and relative URIs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:343
msgid ""
"_uri-template_: URI template according to "
"[RFC6570](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc6570)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:344
msgid ""
"_url_ (deprecated): [URL record](https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-"
"url)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:345
msgid "_email_: email address."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:346
msgid ""
"_hostname_: host name according to "
"[RFC1034](http://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc1034#section-3.5)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:347
msgid "_ipv4_: IP address v4."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:348
msgid "_ipv6_: IP address v6."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:349
msgid ""
"_regex_: tests whether a string is a valid regular expression by passing "
"it to RegExp constructor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:350
msgid ""
"_uuid_: Universally Unique IDentifier according to "
"[RFC4122](http://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc4122)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:351
msgid ""
"_json-pointer_: JSON-pointer according to "
"[RFC6901](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc6901)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:352
msgid ""
"_relative-json-pointer_: relative JSON-pointer according to [this "
"draft](http://tools.ietf.org/html/draft-luff-relative-json-pointer-00)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:354
msgid ""
"__Please note__: JSON Schema draft-07 also defines formats `iri`, `iri-"
"reference`, `idn-hostname` and `idn-email` for URLs, hostnames and emails"
" with international characters. Ajv does not implement these formats. If "
"you create Ajv plugin that implements them please make a PR to mention "
"this plugin here."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:356
msgid ""
"There are two modes of format validation: `fast` and `full`. This mode "
"affects formats `date`, `time`, `date-time`, `uri`, `uri-reference`, and "
"`email`. See [Options](#options) for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:358
msgid ""
"You can add additional formats and replace any of the formats above using"
" [addFormat](#api-addformat) method."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:360
msgid ""
"The option `unknownFormats` allows changing the default behaviour when an"
" unknown format is encountered. In this case Ajv can either fail schema "
"compilation (default) or ignore it (default in versions before 5.0.0). "
"You also can allow specific format(s) that will be ignored. See "
"[Options](#options) for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:362
msgid ""
"You can find regular expressions used for format validation and the "
"sources that were used in [formats.js](https://github.com/ajv-"
"validator/ajv/blob/master/lib/compile/formats.js)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:365
msgid "<a name=\"ref\"></a>Combining schemas with $ref"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:367
msgid ""
"You can structure your validation logic across multiple schema files and "
"have schemas reference each other using `$ref` keyword."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:369 ../../source/ajv_README.md:587
#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:628 ../../source/ajv_README.md:789
msgid "Example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:390
msgid ""
"Now to compile your schema you can either pass all schemas to Ajv "
"instance:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:397
msgid "or use `addSchema` method:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:405
msgid "See [Options](#options) and [addSchema](#api) method."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:407
msgid "__Please note__:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:408
msgid ""
"`$ref` is resolved as the uri-reference using schema $id as the base URI "
"(see the example)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:409
msgid ""
"References can be recursive (and mutually recursive) to implement the "
"schemas for different data structures (such as linked lists, trees, "
"graphs, etc.)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:410
msgid ""
"You don't have to host your schema files at the URIs that you use as "
"schema $id. These URIs are only used to identify the schemas, and "
"according to JSON Schema specification validators should not expect to be"
" able to download the schemas from these URIs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:411
msgid "The actual location of the schema file in the file system is not used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:412
msgid ""
"You can pass the identifier of the schema as the second parameter of "
"`addSchema` method or as a property name in `schemas` option. This "
"identifier can be used instead of (or in addition to) schema $id."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:413
msgid ""
"You cannot have the same $id (or the schema identifier) used for more "
"than one schema - the exception will be thrown."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:414
msgid ""
"You can implement dynamic resolution of the referenced schemas using "
"`compileAsync` method. In this way you can store schemas in any system "
"(files, web, database, etc.) and reference them without explicitly adding"
" to Ajv instance. See [Asynchronous schema compilation](#asynchronous-"
"schema-compilation)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:417
msgid "$data reference"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:419
msgid ""
"With `$data` option you can use values from the validated data as the "
"values for the schema keywords. See [proposal](https://github.com/json-"
"schema-org/json-schema-spec/issues/51) for more information about how it "
"works."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:421
msgid ""
"`$data` reference is supported in the keywords: const, enum, format, "
"maximum/minimum, exclusiveMaximum / exclusiveMinimum, maxLength / "
"minLength, maxItems / minItems, maxProperties / minProperties, "
"formatMaximum / formatMinimum, formatExclusiveMaximum / "
"formatExclusiveMinimum, multipleOf, pattern, required, uniqueItems."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:423
msgid ""
"The value of \"$data\" should be a [JSON-"
"pointer](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc6901) to the data (the root is "
"always the top level data object, even if the $data reference is inside a"
" referenced subschema) or a [relative JSON-"
"pointer](http://tools.ietf.org/html/draft-luff-relative-json-pointer-00) "
"(it is relative to the current point in data; if the $data reference is "
"inside a referenced subschema it cannot point to the data outside of the "
"root level for this subschema)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:425 ../../source/ajv_README.md:479
msgid "Examples."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:427
msgid ""
"This schema requires that the value in property `smaller` is less or "
"equal than the value in the property larger:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:450
msgid ""
"This schema requires that the properties have the same format as their "
"field names:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:466
msgid ""
"`$data` reference is resolved safely - it won't throw even if some "
"property is undefined. If `$data` resolves to `undefined` the validation "
"succeeds (with the exclusion of `const` keyword). If `$data` resolves to "
"incorrect type (e.g. not \"number\" for maximum keyword) the validation "
"fails."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:469
msgid "$merge and $patch keywords"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:471
msgid ""
"With the package [ajv-merge-patch](https://github.com/ajv-validator/ajv-"
"merge-patch) you can use the keywords `$merge` and `$patch` that allow "
"extending JSON Schemas with patches using formats [JSON Merge Patch (RFC "
"7396)](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc7396) and [JSON Patch (RFC "
"6902)](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc6902)."
msgstr ""

