msgid "The schemas above are equivalent to this schema:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:528
msgid ""
"The properties `source` and `with` in the keywords `$merge` and `$patch` "
"can use absolute or relative `$ref` to point to other schemas previously "
"added to the Ajv instance or to the fragments of the current schema."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:530
msgid ""
"See the package [ajv-merge-patch](https://github.com/ajv-validator/ajv-"
"merge-patch) for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:533
msgid "Defining custom keywords"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:535
msgid "The advantages of using custom keywords are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:537
msgid ""
"allow creating validation scenarios that cannot be expressed using JSON "
"Schema"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:538
msgid "simplify your schemas"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:539
msgid "help bringing a bigger part of the validation logic to your schemas"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:540
msgid ""
"make your schemas more expressive, less verbose and closer to your "
"application domain"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:541
msgid ""
"implement custom data processors that modify your data (`modifying` "
"option MUST be used in keyword definition) and/or create side effects "
"while the data is being validated"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:543
msgid ""
"If a keyword is used only for side-effects and its validation result is "
"pre-defined, use option `valid: true/false` in keyword definition to "
"simplify both generated code (no error handling in case of `valid: true`)"
" and your keyword functions (no need to return any validation result)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:545
msgid ""
"The concerns you have to be aware of when extending JSON Schema standard "
"with custom keywords are the portability and understanding of your "
"schemas. You will have to support these custom keywords on other "
"platforms and to properly document these keywords so that everybody can "
"understand them in your schemas."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:547
msgid ""
"You can define custom keywords with [addKeyword](#api-addkeyword) method."
" Keywords are defined on the `ajv` instance level - new instances will "
"not have previously defined keywords."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:549
msgid "Ajv allows defining keywords with:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:550
msgid "validation function"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:551
msgid "compilation function"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:552
msgid "macro function"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:553
msgid ""
"inline compilation function that should return code (as string) that will"
" be inlined in the currently compiled schema."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:555
msgid "Example. `range` and `exclusiveRange` keywords using compiled schema:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:578
msgid ""
"Several custom keywords (typeof, instanceof, range and propertyNames) are"
" defined in [ajv-keywords](https://github.com/ajv-validator/ajv-keywords)"
" package - they can be used for your schemas and as a starting point for "
"your own custom keywords."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:580
msgid ""
"See [Defining custom keywords](https://github.com/ajv-"
"validator/ajv/blob/master/CUSTOM.md) for more details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:583
msgid "Asynchronous schema compilation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:585
msgid ""
"During asynchronous compilation remote references are loaded using "
"supplied function. See `compileAsync` [method](#api-compileAsync) and "
"`loadSchema` [option](#options)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:606
msgid ""
"__Please note__: [Option](#options) `missingRefs` should NOT be set to "
"`\"ignore\"` or `\"fail\"` for asynchronous compilation to work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:609
msgid "Asynchronous validation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:611
msgid ""
"Example in Node.js REPL: https://tonicdev.com/esp/ajv-asynchronous-"
"validation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:613
msgid ""
"You can define custom formats and keywords that perform validation "
"asynchronously by accessing database or some other service. You should "
"add `async: true` in the keyword or format definition (see [addFormat"
"](#api-addformat), [addKeyword](#api-addkeyword) and [Defining custom "
"keywords](#defining-custom-keywords))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:615
msgid ""
"If your schema uses asynchronous formats/keywords or refers to some "
"schema that contains them it should have `\"$async\": true` keyword so "
"that Ajv can compile it correctly. If asynchronous format/keyword or "
"reference to asynchronous schema is used in the schema without `$async` "
"keyword Ajv will throw an exception during schema compilation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:617
msgid ""
"__Please note__: all asynchronous subschemas that are referenced from the"
" current or other schemas should have `\"$async\": true` keyword as well,"
" otherwise the schema compilation will fail."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:619
msgid ""
"Validation function for an asynchronous custom format/keyword should "
"return a promise that resolves with `true` or `false` (or rejects with "
"`new Ajv.ValidationError(errors)` if you want to return custom errors "
"from the keyword function)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:621
msgid ""
"Ajv compiles asynchronous schemas to [es7 async "
"functions](http://tc39.github.io/ecmascript-asyncawait/) that can "
"optionally be transpiled with "
"[nodent](https://github.com/MatAtBread/nodent). Async functions are "
"supported in Node.js 7+ and all modern browsers. You can also supply any "
"other transpiler as a function via `processCode` option. See "
"[Options](#options)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:623
msgid ""
"The compiled validation function has `$async: true` property (if the "
"schema is asynchronous), so you can differentiate these functions if you "
"are using both synchronous and asynchronous schemas."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:625
msgid ""
"Validation result will be a promise that resolves with validated data or "
"rejects with an exception `Ajv.ValidationError` that contains the array "
"of validation errors in `errors` property."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:677
msgid "Using transpilers with asynchronous validation functions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:679
msgid ""
"[ajv-async](https://github.com/ajv-validator/ajv-async) uses "
"[nodent](https://github.com/MatAtBread/nodent) to transpile async "
"functions. To use another transpiler you should separately install it (or"
" load its bundle in the browser)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:682
msgid "Using nodent"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:694
msgid "Using other transpilers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:702
msgid "See [Options](#options)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:705
msgid "Security considerations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:707
msgid ""
"JSON Schema, if properly used, can replace data sanitisation. It doesn't "
"replace other API security considerations. It also introduces additional "
"security aspects to consider."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:710
msgid "Security contact"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:712
msgid ""
"To report a security vulnerability, please use the [Tidelift security "
"contact](https://tidelift.com/security). Tidelift will coordinate the fix"
" and disclosure. Please do NOT report security vulnerabilities via GitHub"
" issues."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:717
msgid "Untrusted schemas"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:719
msgid ""
"Ajv treats JSON schemas as trusted as your application code. This "
"security model is based on the most common use case, when the schemas are"
" static and bundled together with the application."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:721
msgid ""
"If your schemas are received from untrusted sources (or generated from "
"untrusted data) there are several scenarios you need to prevent:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:722
msgid "compiling schemas can cause stack overflow (if they are too deep)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:723
msgid ""
"compiling schemas can be slow (e.g. [#557](https://github.com/ajv-"
"validator/ajv/issues/557))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:724
msgid "validating certain data can be slow"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:726
msgid ""
"It is difficult to predict all the scenarios, but at the very least it "
"may help to limit the size of untrusted schemas (e.g. limit JSON string "
"length) and also the maximum schema object depth (that can be high for "
"relatively small JSON strings). You also may want to mitigate slow "
"regular expressions in `pattern` and `patternProperties` keywords."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:728
msgid ""
"Regardless the measures you take, using untrusted schemas increases "
"security risks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:731
msgid "Circular references in JavaScript objects"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:733
msgid ""
"Ajv does not support schemas and validated data that have circular "
"references in objects. See [issue #802](https://github.com/ajv-"
"validator/ajv/issues/802)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:735
msgid ""
"An attempt to compile such schemas or validate such data would cause "
"stack overflow (or will not complete in case of asynchronous validation)."
" Depending on the parser you use, untrusted data can lead to circular "
"references."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:738
msgid "Security risks of trusted schemas"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:740
msgid ""
"Some keywords in JSON Schemas can lead to very slow validation for "
"certain data. These keywords include (but may be not limited to):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:742
msgid ""
"`pattern` and `format` for large strings - in some cases using "
"`maxLength` can help mitigate it, but certain regular expressions can "
"lead to exponential validation time even with relatively short strings "
"(see [ReDoS attack](#redos-attack))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:743
msgid ""
"`patternProperties` for large property names - use `propertyNames` to "
"mitigate, but some regular expressions can have exponential evaluation "
"time as well."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:744
msgid "`uniqueItems` for large non-scalar arrays - use `maxItems` to mitigate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:746
msgid ""
"__Please note__: The suggestions above to prevent slow validation would "
"only work if you do NOT use `allErrors: true` in production code (using "
"it would continue validation after validation errors)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:748
msgid ""
"You can validate your JSON schemas against [this meta-"
"schema](https://github.com/ajv-validator/ajv/blob/master/lib/refs/json-"
"schema-secure.json) to check that these recommendations are followed:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:760
msgid ""
"__Please note__: following all these recommendation is not a guarantee "
"that validation of untrusted data is safe - it can still lead to some "
"undesirable results."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:763
msgid "Content Security Policies (CSP)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:764
msgid ""
"See [Ajv and Content Security Policies (CSP)](#ajv-and-content-security-"
"policies-csp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:767
msgid "ReDoS attack"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:769
msgid ""
"Certain regular expressions can lead to the exponential evaluation time "
"even with relatively short strings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:771
msgid ""
"Please assess the regular expressions you use in the schemas on their "
"vulnerability to this attack - see [safe-"
"regex](https://github.com/substack/safe-regex), for example."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:773
msgid ""
"__Please note__: some formats that Ajv implements use [regular "
"expressions](https://github.com/ajv-"
"validator/ajv/blob/master/lib/compile/formats.js) that can be vulnerable "
"to ReDoS attack, so if you use Ajv to validate data from untrusted "
"sources __it is strongly recommended__ to consider the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:775
msgid "making assessment of \"format\" implementations in Ajv."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:776
msgid ""
"using `format: 'fast'` option that simplifies some of the regular "
"expressions (although it does not guarantee that they are safe)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:777
msgid ""
"replacing format implementations provided by Ajv with your own "
"implementations of \"format\" keyword that either uses different regular "
"expressions or another approach to format validation. Please see "
"[addFormat](#api-addformat) method."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:778
msgid ""
"disabling format validation by ignoring \"format\" keyword with option "
"`format: false`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:780
msgid ""
"Whatever mitigation you choose, please assume all formats provided by Ajv"
" as potentially unsafe and make your own assessment of their suitability "
"for your validation scenarios."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:783
msgid "Filtering data"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:785
msgid ""
"With [option `removeAdditional`](#options) (added by "
"[andyscott](https://github.com/andyscott)) you can filter data during the"
" validation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:787 ../../source/ajv_README.md:879
#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:938
msgid "This option modifies original data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:821
msgid ""
"If `removeAdditional` option in the example above were `\"all\"` then "
"both `additional1` and `additional2` properties would have been removed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:823
msgid ""
"If the option were `\"failing\"` then property `additional1` would have "
"been removed regardless of its value and property `additional2` would "
"have been removed only if its value were failing the schema in the inner "
"`additionalProperties` (so in the example above it would have stayed "
"because it passes the schema, but any non-number would have been "
"removed)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:825
msgid ""
"__Please note__: If you use `removeAdditional` option with "
"`additionalProperties` keyword inside `anyOf`/`oneOf` keywords your "
"validation can fail with this schema, for example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:849
msgid ""
"The intention of the schema above is to allow objects with either the "
"string property \"foo\" or the integer property \"bar\", but not with "
"both and not with any other properties."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:851
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"With the option `removeAdditional: true` the validation will pass for the"
" object `{ \"foo\": \"abc\"}` but will fail for the object `{\"bar\": "
"1}`. It happens because while the first subschema in `oneOf` is "
"validated, the property `bar` is removed because it is an additional "
"property according to the standard (because it is not included in "
"`properties` keyword in the same schema)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:853
msgid ""
"While this behaviour is unexpected (issues [#129](https://github.com/ajv-"
"validator/ajv/issues/129), [#134](https://github.com/ajv-"
"validator/ajv/issues/134)), it is correct. To have the expected behaviour"
" (both objects are allowed and additional properties are removed) the "
"schema has to be refactored in this way:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:870
msgid ""
"The schema above is also more efficient - it will compile into a faster "
"function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:873
msgid "Assigning defaults"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:875
msgid ""
"With [option `useDefaults`](#options) Ajv will assign values from "
"`default` keyword in the schemas of `properties` and `items` (when it is "
"the array of schemas) to the missing properties and items."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:877
msgid ""
"With the option value `\"empty\"` properties and items equal to `null` or"
" `\"\"` (empty string) will be considered missing and assigned defaults."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:881
msgid ""
"__Please note__: the default value is inserted in the generated "
"validation code as a literal, so the value inserted in the data will be "
"the deep clone of the default in the schema."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:884
msgid "Example 1 (`default` in `properties`):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:905
msgid "Example 2 (`default` in `items`):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:924
msgid "`default` keywords in other cases are ignored:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:926
msgid "not in `properties` or `items` subschemas"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:927
msgid ""
"in schemas inside `anyOf`, `oneOf` and `not` (see "
"[#42](https://github.com/ajv-validator/ajv/issues/42))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:928
msgid "in `if` subschema of `switch` keyword"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:929
msgid "in schemas generated by custom macro keywords"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:931
msgid ""
"The [`strictDefaults` option](#options) customizes Ajv's behavior for the"
" defaults that Ajv ignores (`true` raises an error, and `\"log\"` outputs"
" a warning)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:934
msgid "Coercing data types"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:936
msgid ""
"When you are validating user inputs all your data properties are usually "
"strings. The option `coerceTypes` allows you to have your data types "
"coerced to the types specified in your schema `type` keywords, both to "
"pass the validation and to use the correctly typed data afterwards."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:940
msgid ""
"__Please note__: if you pass a scalar value to the validating function "
"its type will be coerced and it will pass the validation, but the value "
"of the variable you pass won't be updated because scalars are passed by "
"value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:943
msgid "Example 1:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:964
msgid "Example 2 (array coercions):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:983
msgid ""
"The coercion rules, as you can see from the example, are different from "
"JavaScript both to validate user input as expected and to have the "
"coercion reversible (to correctly validate cases where different types "
"are defined in subschemas of \"anyOf\" and other compound keywords)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:985
msgid ""
"See [Coercion rules](https://github.com/ajv-"
"validator/ajv/blob/master/COERCION.md) for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:990
msgid "new Ajv(Object options) -&gt; Object"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:992
msgid "Create Ajv instance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:995
msgid ".compile(Object schema) -&gt; Function&lt;Object data&gt;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:997
msgid "Generate validating function and cache the compiled schema for future use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:999
msgid ""
"Validating function returns a boolean value. This function has properties"
" `errors` and `schema`. Errors encountered during the last validation are"
" assigned to `errors` property (it is assigned `null` if there was no "
"errors). `schema` property contains the reference to the original schema."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1001
msgid ""
"The schema passed to this method will be validated against meta-schema "
"unless `validateSchema` option is false. If schema is invalid, an error "
"will be thrown. See [options](#options)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1004
msgid ""
"<a name=\"api-compileAsync\"></a>.compileAsync(Object schema [, Boolean "
"meta] [, Function callback]) -&gt; Promise"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1006
msgid ""
"Asynchronous version of `compile` method that loads missing remote "
"schemas using asynchronous function in `options.loadSchema`. This "
"function returns a Promise that resolves to a validation function. An "
"optional callback passed to `compileAsync` will be called with 2 "
"parameters: error (or null) and validating function. The returned promise"
" will reject (and the callback will be called with an error) when:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1008
msgid ""
"missing schema can't be loaded (`loadSchema` returns a Promise that "
"rejects)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1009
msgid ""
"a schema containing a missing reference is loaded, but the reference "
"cannot be resolved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1010
msgid "schema (or some loaded/referenced schema) is invalid."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1012
msgid ""
"The function compiles schema and loads the first missing schema (or meta-"
"schema) until all missing schemas are loaded."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1014
msgid ""
"You can asynchronously compile meta-schema by passing `true` as the "
"second parameter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1016
msgid ""
"See example in [Asynchronous compilation](#asynchronous-schema-"
"compilation)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1019
msgid ".validate(Object schema|String key|String ref, data) -&gt; Boolean"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1021
msgid "Validate data using passed schema (it will be compiled and cached)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1023
msgid ""
"Instead of the schema you can use the key that was previously passed to "
"`addSchema`, the schema id if it was present in the schema or any "
"previously resolved reference."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1025
msgid ""
"Validation errors will be available in the `errors` property of Ajv "
"instance (`null` if there were no errors)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1027
msgid ""
"__Please note__: every time this method is called the errors are "
"overwritten so you need to copy them to another variable if you want to "
"use them later."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1029
msgid ""
"If the schema is asynchronous (has `$async` keyword on the top level) "
"this method returns a Promise. See [Asynchronous validation"
"](#asynchronous-validation)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1032
msgid ".addSchema(Array&lt;Object&gt;|Object schema [, String key]) -&gt; Ajv"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1034
msgid ""
"Add schema(s) to validator instance. This method does not compile schemas"
" (but it still validates them). Because of that dependencies can be added"
" in any order and circular dependencies are supported. It also prevents "
"unnecessary compilation of schemas that are containers for other schemas "
"but not used as a whole."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1036
msgid ""
"Array of schemas can be passed (schemas should have ids), the second "
"parameter will be ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1038
msgid ""
"Key can be passed that can be used to reference the schema and will be "
"used as the schema id if there is no id inside the schema. If the key is "
"not passed, the schema id will be used as the key."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1041
msgid ""
"Once the schema is added, it (and all the references inside it) can be "
"referenced in other schemas and used to validate data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1043
msgid ""
"Although `addSchema` does not compile schemas, explicit compilation is "
"not required - the schema will be compiled when it is used first time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1045
msgid ""
"By default the schema is validated against meta-schema before it is "
"added, and if the schema does not pass validation the exception is "
"thrown. This behaviour is controlled by `validateSchema` option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1047
msgid ""
"__Please note__: Ajv uses the [method chaining "
"syntax](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Method_chaining) for all methods "
"with the prefix `add*` and `remove*`. This allows you to do nice things "
"like the following."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1054
msgid ".addMetaSchema(Array&lt;Object&gt;|Object schema [, String key]) -&gt; Ajv"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1056
msgid ""
"Adds meta schema(s) that can be used to validate other schemas. That "
"function should be used instead of `addSchema` because there may be "
"instance options that would compile a meta schema incorrectly (at the "
"moment it is `removeAdditional` option)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1058
msgid ""
"There is no need to explicitly add draft-07 meta schema (http://json-"
"schema.org/draft-07/schema) - it is added by default, unless option "
"`meta` is set to `false`. You only need to use it if you have a changed "
"meta-schema that you want to use to validate your schemas. See "
"`validateSchema`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1061
msgid ""
"<a name=\"api-validateschema\"></a>.validateSchema(Object schema) -&gt; "
"Boolean"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1063
msgid ""
"Validates schema. This method should be used to validate schemas rather "
"than `validate` due to the inconsistency of `uri` format in JSON Schema "
"standard."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1065
msgid ""
"By default this method is called automatically when the schema is added, "
"so you rarely need to use it directly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1067
msgid ""
"If schema doesn't have `$schema` property, it is validated against draft "
"6 meta-schema (option `meta` should not be false)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1069
msgid ""
"If schema has `$schema` property, then the schema with this id (that "
"should be previously added) is used to validate passed schema."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1071
msgid "Errors will be available at `ajv.errors`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1074
msgid ".getSchema(String key) -&gt; Function&lt;Object data&gt;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1076
msgid ""
"Retrieve compiled schema previously added with `addSchema` by the key "
"passed to `addSchema` or by its full reference (id). The returned "
"validating function has `schema` property with the reference to the "
"original schema."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1079
msgid ""
".removeSchema([Object schema|String key|String ref|RegExp pattern]) -&gt;"
" Ajv"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1081
msgid ""
"Remove added/cached schema. Even if schema is referenced by other schemas"
" it can be safely removed as dependent schemas have local references."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1083
msgid "Schema can be removed using:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1084
msgid "key passed to `addSchema`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1085
msgid "it's full reference (id)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1086
msgid "RegExp that should match schema id or key (meta-schemas won't be removed)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1087
msgid ""
"actual schema object that will be stable-stringified to remove schema "
"from cache"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1089
msgid ""
"If no parameter is passed all schemas but meta-schemas will be removed "
"and the cache will be cleared."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1092
msgid ""
"<a name=\"api-addformat\"></a>.addFormat(String name, "
"String|RegExp|Function|Object format) -&gt; Ajv"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1094
msgid ""
"Add custom format to validate strings or numbers. It can also be used to "
"replace pre-defined formats for Ajv instance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1096
msgid "Strings are converted to RegExp."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1098
msgid "Function should return validation result as `true` or `false`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1100
msgid ""
"If object is passed it should have properties `validate`, `compare` and "
"`async`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1102
msgid "_validate_: a string, RegExp or a function as described above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1103
msgid ""
"_compare_: an optional comparison function that accepts two strings and "
"compares them according to the format meaning. This function is used with"
" keywords `formatMaximum`/`formatMinimum` (defined in [ajv-"
"keywords](https://github.com/ajv-validator/ajv-keywords) package). It "
"should return `1` if the first value is bigger than the second value, "
"`-1` if it is smaller and `0` if it is equal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1104
msgid ""
"_async_: an optional `true` value if `validate` is an asynchronous "
"function; in this case it should return a promise that resolves with a "
"value `true` or `false`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1105
msgid ""
"_type_: an optional type of data that the format applies to. It can be "
"`\"string\"` (default) or `\"number\"` (see https://github.com/ajv-"
"validator/ajv/issues/291#issuecomment-259923858). If the type of data is "
"different, the validation will pass."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1107
msgid "Custom formats can be also added via `formats` option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1110
msgid ""
"<a name=\"api-addkeyword\"></a>.addKeyword(String keyword, Object "
"definition) -&gt; Ajv"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1112
msgid "Add custom validation keyword to Ajv instance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1114
msgid ""
"Keyword should be different from all standard JSON Schema keywords and "
"different from previously defined keywords. There is no way to redefine "
"keywords or to remove keyword definition from the instance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1116
msgid ""
"Keyword must start with a letter, `_` or `$`, and may continue with "
"letters, numbers, `_`, `$`, or `-`. It is recommended to use an "
"application-specific prefix for keywords to avoid current and future name"
" collisions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1119
msgid "Example Keywords:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1120
msgid ""
"`\"xyz-example\"`: valid, and uses prefix for the xyz project to avoid "
"name collisions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1121
msgid ""
"`\"example\"`: valid, but not recommended as it could collide with future"
" versions of JSON Schema etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1122
msgid ""
"`\"3-example\"`: invalid as numbers are not allowed to be the first "
"character in a keyword"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1124
msgid "Keyword definition is an object with the following properties:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1126
msgid ""
"_type_: optional string or array of strings with data type(s) that the "
"keyword applies to. If not present, the keyword will apply to all types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1127
msgid "_validate_: validating function"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1128
msgid "_compile_: compiling function"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1129
msgid "_macro_: macro function"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1130
msgid "_inline_: compiling function that returns code (as string)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1131
msgid ""
"_schema_: an optional `false` value used with \"validate\" keyword to not"
" pass schema"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1132
msgid "_metaSchema_: an optional meta-schema for keyword schema"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1133
msgid ""
"_dependencies_: an optional list of properties that must be present in "
"the parent schema - it will be checked during schema compilation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1134
msgid "_modifying_: `true` MUST be passed if keyword modifies data"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1135
msgid ""
"_statements_: `true` can be passed in case inline keyword generates "
"statements (as opposed to expression)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1136
msgid ""
"_valid_: pass `true`/`false` to pre-define validation result, the result "
"returned from validation function will be ignored. This option cannot be "
"used with macro keywords."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1137
msgid ""
"_$data_: an optional `true` value to support [$data reference](#data-"
"reference) as the value of custom keyword. The reference will be resolved"
" at validation time. If the keyword has meta-schema it would be extended "
"to allow $data and it will be used to validate the resolved value. "
"Supporting $data reference requires that keyword has validating function "
"(as the only option or in addition to compile, macro or inline function)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1138
msgid ""
"_async_: an optional `true` value if the validation function is "
"asynchronous (whether it is compiled or passed in _validate_ property); "
"in this case it should return a promise that resolves with a value `true`"
" or `false`. This option is ignored in case of \"macro\" and \"inline\" "
"keywords."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1139
msgid ""
"_errors_: an optional boolean or string `\"full\"` indicating whether "
"keyword returns errors. If this property is not set Ajv will determine if"
" the errors were set in case of failed validation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1141
msgid ""
"_compile_, _macro_ and _inline_ are mutually exclusive, only one should "
"be used at a time. _validate_ can be used separately or in addition to "
"them to support $data reference."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1143
msgid ""
"__Please note__: If the keyword is validating data type that is different"
" from the type(s) in its definition, the validation function will not be "
"called (and expanded macro will not be used), so there is no need to "
"check for data type inside validation function or inside schema returned "
"by macro function (unless you want to enforce a specific type and for "
"some reason do not want to use a separate `type` keyword for that). In "
"the same way as standard keywords work, if the keyword does not apply to "
"the data type being validated, the validation of this keyword will "
"succeed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1145
msgid ""
"See [Defining custom keywords](#defining-custom-keywords) for more "
"details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1148
msgid ".getKeyword(String keyword) -&gt; Object|Boolean"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1150
msgid ""
"Returns custom keyword definition, `true` for pre-defined keywords and "
"`false` if the keyword is unknown."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1153
msgid ".removeKeyword(String keyword) -&gt; Ajv"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1155
msgid "Removes custom or pre-defined keyword so you can redefine them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1157
msgid ""
"While this method can be used to extend pre-defined keywords, it can also"
" be used to completely change their meaning - it may lead to unexpected "
"results."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1159
msgid ""
"__Please note__: schemas compiled before the keyword is removed will "
"continue to work without changes. To recompile schemas use `removeSchema`"
" method and compile them again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1162
msgid ".errorsText([Array&lt;Object&gt; errors [, Object options]]) -&gt; String"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1164
msgid "Returns the text with all errors in a String."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1166
msgid ""
"Options can have properties `separator` (string used to separate errors, "
"\", \" by default) and `dataVar` (the variable name that dataPaths are "
"prefixed with, \"data\" by default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1169
msgid "Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1171
msgid "Defaults:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1223
msgid "Validation and reporting options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1225
msgid ""
"_$data_: support [$data references](#data-reference). Draft 6 meta-schema"
" that is added by default will be extended to allow them. If you want to "
"use another meta-schema you need to use $dataMetaSchema method to add "
"support for $data reference. See [API](#api)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1226
msgid ""
"_allErrors_: check all rules collecting all errors. Default is to return "
"after the first error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1227
msgid ""
"_verbose_: include the reference to the part of the schema (`schema` and "
"`parentSchema`) and validated data in errors (false by default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1228
msgid ""
"_$comment_ (NEW in Ajv version 6.0): log or pass the value of `$comment` "
"keyword to a function. Option values:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1229
msgid "`false` (default): ignore $comment keyword."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1230
msgid "`true`: log the keyword value to console."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1231
msgid ""
"function: pass the keyword value, its schema path and root schema to the "
"specified function"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1232
msgid ""
"_jsonPointers_: set `dataPath` property of errors using [JSON "
"Pointers](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc6901) instead of JavaScript "
"property access notation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1233
msgid "_uniqueItems_: validate `uniqueItems` keyword (true by default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1234
msgid ""
"_unicode_: calculate correct length of strings with unicode pairs (true "
"by default). Pass `false` to use `.length` of strings that is faster, but"
" gives \"incorrect\" lengths of strings with unicode pairs - each unicode"
" pair is counted as two characters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1235
msgid ""
"_nullable_: support keyword \"nullable\" from [Open API 3 "
"specification](https://swagger.io/docs/specification/data-models/data-"
"types/)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1236
msgid "_format_: formats validation mode. Option values:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1237
msgid ""
"`\"fast\"` (default) - simplified and fast validation (see "
"[Formats](#formats) for details of which formats are available and "
"affected by this option)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1238
msgid ""
"`\"full\"` - more restrictive and slow validation. E.g., 25:00:00 and "
"2015/14/33 will be invalid time and date in 'full' mode but it will be "
"valid in 'fast' mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1239
msgid "`false` - ignore all format keywords."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1240
msgid ""
"_formats_: an object with custom formats. Keys and values will be passed "
"to `addFormat` method."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1241
msgid ""
"_keywords_: an object with custom keywords. Keys and values will be "
"passed to `addKeyword` method."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1242
msgid "_unknownFormats_: handling of unknown formats. Option values:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1243
msgid ""
"`true` (default) - if an unknown format is encountered the exception is "
"thrown during schema compilation. If `format` keyword value is [$data "
"reference](#data-reference) and it is unknown the validation will fail."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1244
msgid ""
"`[String]` - an array of unknown format names that will be ignored. This "
"option can be used to allow usage of third party schemas with format(s) "
"for which you don't have definitions, but still fail if another unknown "
"format is used. If `format` keyword value is [$data reference](#data-"
"reference) and it is not in this array the validation will fail."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1245
msgid ""
"`\"ignore\"` - to log warning during schema compilation and always pass "
"validation (the default behaviour in versions before 5.0.0). This option "
"is not recommended, as it allows to mistype format name and it won't be "
"validated without any error message. This behaviour is required by JSON "
"Schema specification."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1246
msgid ""
"_schemas_: an array or object of schemas that will be added to the "
"instance. In case you pass the array the schemas must have IDs in them. "
"When the object is passed the method `addSchema(value, key)` will be "
"called for each schema in this object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1247
msgid ""
"_logger_: sets the logging method. Default is the global `console` object"
" that should have methods `log`, `warn` and `error`. See [Error logging"
"](#error-logging). Option values:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1248
msgid ""
"custom logger - it should have methods `log`, `warn` and `error`. If any "
"of these methods is missing an exception will be thrown."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1249
msgid "`false` - logging is disabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1252
msgid "Referenced schema options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1254
msgid ""
"_schemaId_: this option defines which keywords are used as schema URI. "
"Option value:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1255
msgid ""
"`\"$id\"` (default) - only use `$id` keyword as schema URI (as specified "
"in JSON Schema draft-06/07), ignore `id` keyword (if it is present a "
"warning will be logged)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1256
msgid ""
"`\"id\"` - only use `id` keyword as schema URI (as specified in JSON "
"Schema draft-04), ignore `$id` keyword (if it is present a warning will "
"be logged)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1257
msgid ""
"`\"auto\"` - use both `$id` and `id` keywords as schema URI. If both are "
"present (in the same schema object) and different the exception will be "
"thrown during schema compilation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1258
msgid "_missingRefs_: handling of missing referenced schemas. Option values:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1259
msgid ""
"`true` (default) - if the reference cannot be resolved during compilation"
" the exception is thrown. The thrown error has properties `missingRef` "
"(with hash fragment) and `missingSchema` (without it). Both properties "
"are resolved relative to the current base id (usually schema id, unless "
"it was substituted)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1260
msgid "`\"ignore\"` - to log error during compilation and always pass validation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1261
msgid ""
"`\"fail\"` - to log error and successfully compile schema but fail "
"validation if this rule is checked."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1262
msgid ""
"_extendRefs_: validation of other keywords when `$ref` is present in the "
"schema. Option values:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1263
msgid ""
"`\"ignore\"` (default) - when `$ref` is used other keywords are ignored "
"(as per [JSON Reference](https://tools.ietf.org/html/draft-pbryan-zyp-"
"json-ref-03#section-3) standard). A warning will be logged during the "
"schema compilation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1264
msgid ""
"`\"fail\"` (recommended) - if other validation keywords are used together"
" with `$ref` the exception will be thrown when the schema is compiled. "
"This option is recommended to make sure schema has no keywords that are "
"ignored, which can be confusing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1265
msgid ""
"`true` - validate all keywords in the schemas with `$ref` (the default "
"behaviour in versions before 5.0.0)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1266
msgid ""
"_loadSchema_: asynchronous function that will be used to load remote "
"schemas when `compileAsync` [method](#api-compileAsync) is used and some "
"reference is missing (option `missingRefs` should NOT be 'fail' or "
"'ignore'). This function should accept remote schema uri as a parameter "
"and return a Promise that resolves to a schema. See example in "
"[Asynchronous compilation](#asynchronous-schema-compilation)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1269
msgid "Options to modify validated data"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1271
msgid ""
"_removeAdditional_: remove additional properties - see example in "
"[Filtering data](#filtering-data). This option is not used if schema is "
"added with `addMetaSchema` method. Option values:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1272
msgid "`false` (default) - not to remove additional properties"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1273
msgid ""
"`\"all\"` - all additional properties are removed, regardless of "
"`additionalProperties` keyword in schema (and no validation is made for "
"them)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1274
msgid ""
"`true` - only additional properties with `additionalProperties` keyword "
"equal to `false` are removed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1275
msgid ""
"`\"failing\"` - additional properties that fail schema validation will be"
" removed (where `additionalProperties` keyword is `false` or schema)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1276
msgid ""
"_useDefaults_: replace missing or undefined properties and items with the"
" values from corresponding `default` keywords. Default behaviour is to "
"ignore `default` keywords. This option is not used if schema is added "
"with `addMetaSchema` method. See examples in [Assigning defaults"
"](#assigning-defaults). Option values:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1277
msgid "`false` (default) - do not use defaults"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1278
msgid "`true` - insert defaults by value (object literal is used)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1279
msgid ""
"`\"empty\"` - in addition to missing or undefined, use defaults for "
"properties and items that are equal to `null` or `\"\"` (an empty "
"string)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1280
msgid ""
"`\"shared\"` (deprecated) - insert defaults by reference. If the default "
"is an object, it will be shared by all instances of validated data. If "
"you modify the inserted default in the validated data, it will be "
"modified in the schema as well."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1281
msgid ""
"_coerceTypes_: change data type of data to match `type` keyword. See the "
"example in [Coercing data types](#coercing-data-types) and [coercion "
"rules](https://github.com/ajv-validator/ajv/blob/master/COERCION.md). "
"Option values:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1282
msgid "`false` (default) - no type coercion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1283
msgid "`true` - coerce scalar data types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1284
msgid ""
"`\"array\"` - in addition to coercions between scalar types, coerce "
"scalar data to an array with one element and vice versa (as required by "
"the schema)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1287
msgid "Strict mode options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1289
msgid ""
"_strictDefaults_: report ignored `default` keywords in schemas. Option "
"values:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1290
msgid "`false` (default) - ignored defaults are not reported"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1291
msgid "`true` - if an ignored default is present, throw an error"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1292
msgid "`\"log\"` - if an ignored default is present, log warning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1293
msgid "_strictKeywords_: report unknown keywords in schemas. Option values:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1294
msgid "`false` (default) - unknown keywords are not reported"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1295
msgid "`true` - if an unknown keyword is present, throw an error"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1296
msgid "`\"log\"` - if an unknown keyword is present, log warning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1297
msgid ""
"_strictNumbers_: validate numbers strictly, failing validation for NaN "
"and Infinity. Option values:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1298
msgid "`false` (default) - NaN or Infinity will pass validation for numeric types"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1299
msgid "`true` - NaN or Infinity will not pass validation for numeric types"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1301
msgid "Asynchronous validation options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1303
msgid ""
"_transpile_: Requires [ajv-async](https://github.com/ajv-validator/ajv-"
"async) package. It determines whether Ajv transpiles compiled "
"asynchronous validation function. Option values:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1304
msgid ""
"`undefined` (default) - transpile with "
"[nodent](https://github.com/MatAtBread/nodent) if async functions are not"
" supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1305
msgid "`true` - always transpile with nodent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1306
msgid ""
"`false` - do not transpile; if async functions are not supported an "
"exception will be thrown."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1309
msgid "Advanced options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1311
msgid ""
"_meta_: add [meta-schema](http://json-schema.org/documentation.html) so "
"it can be used by other schemas (true by default). If an object is "
"passed, it will be used as the default meta-schema for schemas that have "
"no `$schema` keyword. This default meta-schema MUST have `$schema` "
"keyword."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1312
msgid ""
"_validateSchema_: validate added/compiled schemas against meta-schema "
"(true by default). `$schema` property in the schema can be http://json-"
"schema.org/draft-07/schema or absent (draft-07 meta-schema will be used) "
"or can be a reference to the schema previously added with `addMetaSchema`"
" method. Option values:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1313
msgid "`true` (default) -  if the validation fails, throw the exception."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1314
msgid "`\"log\"` - if the validation fails, log error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1315
msgid "`false` - skip schema validation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1316
msgid ""
"_addUsedSchema_: by default methods `compile` and `validate` add schemas "
"to the instance if they have `$id` (or `id`) property that doesn't start "
"with \"#\". If `$id` is present and it is not unique the exception will "
"be thrown. Set this option to `false` to skip adding schemas to the "
"instance and the `$id` uniqueness check when these methods are used. This"
" option does not affect `addSchema` method."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1317
msgid "_inlineRefs_: Affects compilation of referenced schemas. Option values:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1318
msgid ""
"`true` (default) - the referenced schemas that don't have refs in them "
"are inlined, regardless of their size - that substantially improves "
"performance at the cost of the bigger size of compiled schema functions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1319
msgid ""
"`false` - to not inline referenced schemas (they will be compiled as "
"separate functions)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1320
msgid ""
"integer number - to limit the maximum number of keywords of the schema "
"that will be inlined."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1321
msgid ""
"_passContext_: pass validation context to custom keyword functions. If "
"this option is `true` and you pass some context to the compiled "
"validation function with `validate.call(context, data)`, the `context` "
"will be available as `this` in your custom keywords. By default `this` is"
" Ajv instance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1322
msgid ""
"_loopRequired_: by default `required` keyword is compiled into a single "
"expression (or a sequence of statements in `allErrors` mode). In case of "
"a very large number of properties in this keyword it may result in a very"
" big validation function. Pass integer to set the number of properties "
"above which `required` keyword will be validated in a loop - smaller "
"validation function size but also worse performance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1323
msgid ""
"_ownProperties_: by default Ajv iterates over all enumerable object "
"properties; when this option is `true` only own enumerable object "
"properties (i.e. found directly on the object rather than on its "
"prototype) are iterated. Contributed by @mbroadst."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1324
msgid ""
"_multipleOfPrecision_: by default `multipleOf` keyword is validated by "
"comparing the result of division with parseInt() of that result. It works"
" for dividers that are bigger than 1. For small dividers such as 0.01 the"
" result of the division is usually not integer (even when it should be "
"integer, see issue [#84](https://github.com/ajv-"
"validator/ajv/issues/84)). If you need to use fractional dividers set "
"this option to some positive integer N to have `multipleOf` validated "
"using this formula: `Math.abs(Math.round(division) - division) < 1e-N` "
"(it is slower but allows for float arithmetics deviations)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1325
msgid ""
"_errorDataPath_ (deprecated): set `dataPath` to point to 'object' "
"(default) or to 'property' when validating keywords `required`, "
"`additionalProperties` and `dependencies`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1326
msgid ""
"_messages_: Include human-readable messages in errors. `true` by default."
" `false` can be passed when custom messages are used (e.g. with [ajv-"
"i18n](https://github.com/ajv-validator/ajv-i18n))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1327
msgid ""
"_sourceCode_: add `sourceCode` property to validating function (for "
"debugging; this code can be different from the result of toString call)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1328
msgid ""
"_processCode_: an optional function to process generated code before it "
"is passed to Function constructor. It can be used to either beautify (the"
" validating function is generated without line-breaks) or to transpile "
"code. Starting from version 5.0.0 this option replaced options:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1329
msgid ""
"`beautify` that formatted the generated function using [js-"
"beautify](https://github.com/beautify-web/js-beautify). If you want to "
"beautify the generated code pass a function calling `require('js-"
"beautify').js_beautify` as `processCode: code => js_beautify(code)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1330
msgid ""
"`transpile` that transpiled asynchronous validation function. You can "
"still use `transpile` option with [ajv-async](https://github.com/ajv-"
"validator/ajv-async) package. See [Asynchronous validation"
"](#asynchronous-validation) for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1331
msgid ""
"_cache_: an optional instance of cache to store compiled schemas using "
"stable-stringified schema as a key. For example, set-associative cache "
"[sacjs](https://github.com/epoberezkin/sacjs) can be used. If not passed "
"then a simple hash is used which is good enough for the common use case "
"(a limited number of statically defined schemas). Cache should have "
"methods `put(key, value)`, `get(key)`, `del(key)` and `clear()`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1332
msgid ""
"_serialize_: an optional function to serialize schema to cache key. Pass "
"`false` to use schema itself as a key (e.g., if WeakMap used as a cache)."
" By default [fast-json-stable-stringify](https://github.com/epoberezkin"
"/fast-json-stable-stringify) is used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1333
msgid ""
"_regExp_: an optional function to create RegExp objects. This allows "
"using a custom RegExp engine (e.g., [RE2](https://github.com/uhop/node-"
"re2)) to mitigate ReDoS attacks. The function must have the signature "
"`(pattern: string) => RegExpLike` where `RegExpLike` is an object with a "
"`test(string) => boolean` method. Example with RE2:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1337
msgid "By default (`undefined`), native `RegExp` constructor is used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1340
msgid "Validation errors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1342
msgid ""
"In case of validation failure, Ajv assigns the array of errors to "
"`errors` property of validation function (or to `errors` property of Ajv "
"instance when `validate` or `validateSchema` methods were called). In "
"case of [asynchronous validation](#asynchronous-validation), the returned"
" promise is rejected with exception `Ajv.ValidationError` that has "
"`errors` property."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1345
msgid "Error objects"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1347
msgid "Each error is an object with the following properties:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1349
msgid "_keyword_: validation keyword."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1350
msgid ""
"_dataPath_: the path to the part of the data that was validated. By "
"default `dataPath` uses JavaScript property access notation (e.g., "
"`\".prop[1].subProp\"`). When the option `jsonPointers` is true (see "
"[Options](#options)) `dataPath` will be set using JSON pointer standard "
"(e.g., `\"/prop/1/subProp\"`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1351
msgid ""
"_schemaPath_: the path (JSON-pointer as a URI fragment) to the schema of "
"the keyword that failed validation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1352
msgid ""
"_params_: the object with the additional information about error that can"
" be used to create custom error messages (e.g., using [ajv-"
"i18n](https://github.com/ajv-validator/ajv-i18n) package). See below for "
"parameters set by all keywords."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1353
msgid ""
"_message_: the standard error message (can be excluded with option "
"`messages` set to false)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1354
msgid "_schema_: the schema of the keyword (added with `verbose` option)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1355
msgid ""
"_parentSchema_: the schema containing the keyword (added with `verbose` "
"option)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1356
msgid "_data_: the data validated by the keyword (added with `verbose` option)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1358
msgid ""
"__Please note__: `propertyNames` keyword schema validation errors have an"
" additional property `propertyName`, `dataPath` points to the object. "
"After schema validation for each property name, if it is invalid an "
"additional error is added with the property `keyword` equal to "
"`\"propertyNames\"`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1361
msgid "Error parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1363
msgid ""
"Properties of `params` object in errors depend on the keyword that failed"
" validation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1365
msgid ""
"`maxItems`, `minItems`, `maxLength`, `minLength`, `maxProperties`, "
"`minProperties` - property `limit` (number, the schema of the keyword)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1366
msgid ""
"`additionalItems` - property `limit` (the maximum number of allowed items"
" in case when `items` keyword is an array of schemas and "
"`additionalItems` is false)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1367
msgid ""
"`additionalProperties` - property `additionalProperty` (the property not "
"used in `properties` and `patternProperties` keywords)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1368
msgid "`dependencies` - properties:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1369
msgid "`property` (dependent property),"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1370
msgid ""
"`missingProperty` (required missing dependency - only the first one is "
"reported currently)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1371
msgid "`deps` (required dependencies, comma separated list as a string),"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1372
msgid "`depsCount` (the number of required dependencies)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1373
msgid "`format` - property `format` (the schema of the keyword)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1374
msgid "`maximum`, `minimum` - properties:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1375
msgid "`limit` (number, the schema of the keyword),"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1376
msgid ""
"`exclusive` (boolean, the schema of `exclusiveMaximum` or "
"`exclusiveMinimum`),"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1377
msgid ""
"`comparison` (string, comparison operation to compare the data to the "
"limit, with the data on the left and the limit on the right; can be "
"\"<\", \"<=\", \">\", \">=\")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1378
msgid "`multipleOf` - property `multipleOf` (the schema of the keyword)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1379
msgid "`pattern` - property `pattern` (the schema of the keyword)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1380
msgid ""
"`required` - property `missingProperty` (required property that is "
"missing)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1381
msgid "`propertyNames` - property `propertyName` (an invalid property name)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1382
msgid ""
"`patternRequired` (in ajv-keywords) - property `missingPattern` (required"
" pattern that did not match any property)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1383
msgid ""
"`type` - property `type` (required type(s), a string, can be a comma-"
"separated list)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1384
msgid "`uniqueItems` - properties `i` and `j` (indices of duplicate items)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1385
msgid ""
"`const` - property `allowedValue` pointing to the value (the schema of "
"the keyword)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1386
msgid ""
"`enum` - property `allowedValues` pointing to the array of values (the "
"schema of the keyword)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1387
msgid "`$ref` - property `ref` with the referenced schema URI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1388
msgid ""
"`oneOf` - property `passingSchemas` (array of indices of passing schemas,"
" null if no schema passes)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1389
msgid ""
"custom keywords (in case keyword definition doesn't create errors) - "
"property `keyword` (the keyword name)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1392
msgid "Error logging"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1394
msgid ""
"Using the `logger` option when initiallizing Ajv will allow you to define"
" custom logging. Here you can build upon the exisiting logging. The use "
"of other logging packages is supported as long as the package or its "
"associated wrapper exposes the required methods. If any of the required "
"methods are missing an exception will be thrown."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ajv_README.md:1395
msgid "**Required Methods**: `log`, `warn`, `error`"
msgstr ""

